#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:4
msgid ":index:`CD Lookup Options <configuration; cd lookup>`"
msgstr ":index:`Opties voor cd’s opzoeken <configuratie; cd’s opzoeken>`"

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:6
msgid ""
"This section allows you to select which CD ROM device to use by default for "
"looking up a CD."
msgstr ""
"In dit gedeelte kan je instellen welk cd-romstation standaard wordt gebruikt "
"om een cd op te zoeken."

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:19
msgid ""
"When the \"Read ISRCs from CD\" option is enabled, ISRCs will be read from "
"the CD during the disc lookup. The ISRCs will be added to the file metadata "
"when the CD is read, and will be used when looking up releases on "
"MusicBrainz. Note that the code library used does not support reading ISRCs "
"from CDs on some operating system platforms, so this option will not be "
"available on those platforms. The three main platforms (Windows, Linux, and "
"macOS) are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:23
msgid ""
"Not all CD drives support reading ISRCs, and some may significantly slow "
"down the disc reads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:25
msgid ""
"Not all CDs have ISRCs, and some readers may not be able to read them even "
"if they are present on the CD. It is also possible that the ISRCs on the CD "
"are not correct or have been read incorrectly, so you should always check "
"the ISRCs before submitting them to the MusicBrainz database."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:28
msgid "Platform-specific details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:30
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Windows:**"
msgstr "**Windows:**"

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:32
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Picard has a pulldown menu listing the various CD drives it has found. Pull "
"down the menu and select the drive you want to use by default. You can "
"override this setting by clicking on :menuselection:`\"Tools --> Lookup CD..."
"\"` and selecting the desired device from the list of available devices."
msgstr ""
"Op Windows- en Linux-systemen kan je deze instelling negeren door "
"op :menuselection:`‘Hulpmiddelen --> Cd opzoeken’` te klikken en het "
"gewenste apparaat te selecteren in de lijst met beschikbare apparaten."

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:34
#, fuzzy
msgid "**Linux:**"
msgstr "**Linux:**"

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:36
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Picard has a pulldown menu like in Windows for the CD Lookup option. If "
"you're using an older version of Picard with a text field, you should enter "
"the device name (typically ``/dev/cdrom``). You can override this setting by "
"clicking on :menuselection:`\"Tools --> Lookup CD...\"` and selecting the "
"desired device from the list of available devices."
msgstr ""
"Op Windows- en Linux-systemen kan je deze instelling negeren door "
"op :menuselection:`‘Hulpmiddelen --> Cd opzoeken’` te klikken en het "
"gewenste apparaat te selecteren in de lijst met beschikbare apparaten."

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:38
msgid "**macOS:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:40
msgid ""
"In macOS, the CD Lookup option is currently a text field. The device is "
"usually ``/dev/rdisk1``. If that doesn't work, one way is to simply keep "
"increasing the number (e.g. ``/dev/rdisk2``) until it does work. A less "
"trial and error method is to open \"Terminal\" and type ``mount``. The "
"output should include a line such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:46
msgid ""
"You need to replace ``/dev/disk`` with ``/dev/rdisk``. For example, if it "
"says ``/dev/disk2`` you should enter ``/dev/rdisk2`` in Picard's preferences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:48
msgid "**Other platforms:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:50
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"On other platforms, the CD Lookup option is a text field and you should "
"enter the path to the CD drive here."
msgstr ""
"Op andere platformen is de optie Cd opzoeken een tekstveld waarin je het pad "
"naar het cd-station moet invullen."

#: ../../config/options_cdlookup.rst:52
msgid ""
"Note that the code library used does not support reading ISRCs from CDs on "
"some operating system platforms, so this option will not be available on "
"those platforms."
msgstr ""

